CORE
oob.i
--arch x86_64 --os linux --pointer-check
^EXIT=10$
^SIGNAL=0$
^\[main\.pointer_dereference\.1\] line 14 dereference failure: pointer outside object bounds in b\[\(signed long int\)7\]: FAILURE$
^VERIFICATION FAILED$
--
^warning: ignoring
--
From #9304: the unnamed bit-field used to raise the alignment, and thereby the
size, of struct A to 4, so that the out-of-bounds write went unnoticed.
